\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Write a program to read a string of 10 digit number , check whether the string contains a 10 digit number in the format XXX-XXX-XXXX where 'X' is a digit.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Include a class UserMainCode with a static method validateNumber which accepts a string as input .
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The return type of the output should be 1 if the string meets the above specified format . In case the number does not meet the specified format then return -1 as output.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Create a class Main which would get the input as a String of numbers and call the static methodvalidateNumber present in the UserMainCode.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Input and Output Format:
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Input consists of a string.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Output is a string specifying the given string is valid or not .
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Refer sample output for formatting specifications.
