ng  and to test whether first and last character are same. The string is said to be be valid if the 1st and last character are the same. Else the string is said to be invalid.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Include a class UserMainCode with a static method checkCharacters which accepts a string as input .
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The return type of this method is an int.  Output should be 1 if the first character and last character are same . If they are different then return -1 as output.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Create a class Main which would get the input as a string and call th\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 e static method checkCharacterspresent in the UserMainCode.
